# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
#
# EXCEPTION for this project: app/keystore/upload-keystore.jks and
# key.properties ARE committed on purpose. The alternative — signing
# release builds with the ambient per-machine debug keystore — silently
# changes the signing key every time the dev environment is rebuilt,
# which Android's installer then treats as a totally different app
# ("package conflicts with an existing package" on every update). This
# keystore secures nothing sensitive (no Play Store listing, no paid
# distribution) — its only job is staying the same build to build.
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
!key.properties
!app/keystore/upload-keystore.jks
